gr-bbc
======

Baird, Bahn and Collins' concurrent codec for GNU Radio 3.10+.

The Python namespace is "bbc":

    import bbc

    encoder = bbc.Encoder(message_length=8, codeword_length=1024)
    decoder = bbc.Decoder(message_length=8, codeword_length=1024)
    print(decoder.decode(encoder.encode(b"GRCon26!")))

The blocks are bbc.bbc_encoder, bbc.bbc_decoder, bbc.OOKModulator and
bbc.OOKDemodulator; each carries its own docstring, and the GRC block
definitions carry the same text in their documentation tab.

    help(bbc)

The module is pure Python, so there is no Doxygen documentation to build.
bbc.codec and bbc.glowworm import nothing from GNU Radio and can be used
from a plain script.

See README.md at the top of the source tree for the codec's properties and
its limitations, and CHANGELOG.md for what changed in the 3.10 port.
